Battle engine changes

Watch Mode must use the real Battle simulation.

Do not make a separate WatchBattle simulation.

Extend Battle cleanly so its controller configuration can represent:

Quick Battle

* P1 → PlayerController
* P2 → CombatAIController

Watch Mode

* P1 → CombatAIController
* P2 → CombatAIController

Both Watch CPUs use the selected difficulty.

Their fighter definitions remain independent:

CPU 1 → selected cpu1CharacterId
CPU 2 → selected cpu2CharacterId

Everything else remains normal Battle behavior:

* 99-second timer/current configured round time
* first to the configured points-to-win
* Void scoring
* respawns
* Launch Point
* Energy
* shields
* charged attacks
* clones
* projectiles
* stage physics
* camera
* hit FX
* result rules
* rematches
